📋 Project Origins & Strategic Decision
Initial Challenge
We started with a basic PSA signing system (psa.astro) that provided functional document signing but lacked the premium user experience required for USRad's aggressive 1,500 imaging center recruitment strategy. The original system, while working, had:

Basic UI with minimal user guidance
Limited visual feedback during the signing process
No progressive disclosure or step-by-step guidance
Simple iframe embedding without advanced error handling

Strategic Decision: Enhanced PSA Development
We decided to develop an enhanced version (enhanced-psa.astro + EnhancedPSAComponent.jsx) for several critical business reasons:

Premium Brand Positioning: USRad needs to demonstrate technology leadership over competitors like RadNet ($740M) and SimonMed ($600M PE backing)
Provider Confidence Building: First impressions during onboarding directly impact provider commitment to completing the 5-step process
Scalability Requirements: Enhanced error handling and user guidance reduce support tickets during rapid scaling
Professional Differentiation: Enterprise-grade UX justifies choosing USRad over basic competitor platforms


